{
  "title": "Record gateway calls that fail before an upstream response",
  "description": "In an existing completed Commander game, Codex recorded 98 MCP calls but player-tools.jsonl contains only 97 responses. A choose_action timeout at about 180 seconds was absent from gateway trace. In windows/game_tool_gateway.py Handler.do_POST, opener.open/read precedes tracing and only HTTPError is handled; timeout/transport exceptions skip the record. Record every attempt and its terminal status/duration with a safe error category and request ID, including disconnect/timeout/cancellation, without credentials or auth data. Do not silently retry mutation calls: an action may have executed before a response was lost. Acceptance: fake-upstream timeout and disconnect tests assert a single terminal trace per attempted call, coherent counts and safe error handling. This is an observability/reliability problem, not evidence of a runaway model retry loop. See doc/windows-subscription-usage-audit.md.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
